{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And you, encamp outside the camp.</b> That they should not enter the Temple court, because of the Divine Presence that dwells within it." "<b>Whoever kills a soul.</b> And touches it by way of the sword's being joined to him, analogous to one who touches, to exclude one who shoots an arrow at it and kills it, who does not contract impurity." "<b>You shall purify yourselves.</b> With the waters of the purifying waters (מי נדה) according to the law of one impure through corpse-impurity, for even though gentiles do not impart impurity in a tent (אהל), they do impart impurity by contact (מגע) and by carrying (משא)." "<b>You and your captives.</b> Once they convert, they receive impurity and require sprinkling (הזאה)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:21.021611060Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}